Finding: {"title":"Cross-tenant PII/financial data leak: 30+ GET endpoints resolve flightSchoolId from the URL locationId without verifying it belongs to the caller's own org","severity":"CRITICAL","area":"Multi-tenant isolation / API security","files":["src/server/routes/routes-locations.ts"],"detail":"The helper resolveFlightSchoolFromLocation() (line 2963) is documented as 'tenant-guard-exempt: pure resolver — every caller compares the result to the session orgId before using it.' That invariant is violated by ~34 read routes and 2 write routes that call it but never compare the resolved flightSchoolId against the caller's session orgId (via resolveOrgIdFromSession). Confirmed call sites lacking the check include: GET /locations/:locationId/students/:studentId/payment-cards (line 23400, returns Stripe payment card data), .../payment-history (24457), .../documents (25856), .../logbook (11092), .../audit (10337), .../holds (10601), .../certificates (43119), .../notes (36751), .../endorsements (36393), .../invoices (16942), .../lenders (24415), .../flags (42900); GET /locations/:locationId/enrollments (6555) and /classes/:classId/enrollments (6614) — student names/emails; GET /locations/:locationId/payroll (37475) — instructor pay data, only requireAuth (any role); GET /locations/:locationId/admins (40336) — admin names/emails, only requireAuth; GET /locations/:locationId/customers (39793) and /crm-contacts (43264); GET .../instructors/document-compliance* (25736, 25765, 25812) and /students/document-compliance* (8617, 8693, 25594); POST /locations/:locationId/students/:studentId/force-document-upload (26666, requireAdmin) — writes to another org's student record; POST /locations/:locationId/notifications (42723) — writes a notification into another org's location. All of these only validate isUuid(locationId) (format) and that flightSchoolId is non-null (location exists) — never that it equals the requester's own organization. Contrast with correctly-guarded sibling routes in the same file, e.g. POST /locations/:locationId/customers (39834) and PUT/DELETE /locations/:id (2792, 2839), which use findByIdUnscoped + loc.flightSchoolId !== orgId checks.","impact":"Any authenticated user of ANY tenant (school) — including a low-privilege student or instructor account — can read another tenant's student payment cards, payment history, document uploads, logbooks, audit trails, holds, certificates, private notes, endorsements, invoices, lender info, compliance flags, instructor payroll figures, and the school's admin roster, by supplying an arbitrary valid locationId/studentId UUID pair for a different organization. Two write paths let a cross-tenant admin force a document-upload flag onto another school's student, and any authenticated user can inject spam/phishing notifications into another school's location. This is a direct multi-tenant data-isolation breach (aviation training/PII/financial data) and would violate FAA-adjacent compliance and PDD-005 (auth middleware centralization) intent.","recommendation":"Add the standard org-ownership check to every listed call site: resolve authUser/orgId via resolveOrgIdFromSession, then compare flightSchoolId !== orgId and return 404 on mismatch, immediately after resolving flightSchoolId. Given the number of affected sites, replace resolveFlightSchoolFromLocation with a single helper resolveAndVerifyFlightSchool(locationId, authUser, c) that performs both steps atomically, then update all 61 call sites so no caller can forget the check again. Also correct the misleading 'tenant-guard-exempt' comment at line 2963 once callers are fixed — it currently asserts a false invariant that let this drift in unnoticed.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

